% Cervical Traction Devices: LCD L33823 and its Policy Article A52476 (DME
% MACs). A policy program of the DMEPOS model: it includes dmepos.le
% (orders, delivery, benefit category, continued need, refills) and states
% when a claim for a cervical traction device is REASONABLE AND NECESSARY:
% the criteria 1 and 2 of every device (a musculoskeletal or neurologic
% impairment requiring traction equipment; the appropriate use demonstrated
% and the selected device tolerated), which suffice for the over-the-door
% device (E0860); and, for the higher-force devices — the free-standing
% pneumatic frame (E0849) and the device without a door, frame or stand
% (E0855) — one of the additional criteria A, B or C (a treated
% temporomandibular joint dysfunction; a distortion of the lower jaw or neck
% anatomy such that a chin halter cannot be used; the treating practitioner
% ordering or documenting more than 20 pounds of traction in the home). The
% headboard (E0840) and free-standing frame (E0850) devices have "no proven
% clinical advantage" over the over-the-door one and are denied; the
% ambulatory device (E0856) is denied: no rule concludes them.
%
% How the criteria are read. Criterion 1 and criterion B are clinical
% findings about the beneficiary made by the treating practitioner and
% accepted or rejected on review: each is the judged template of dmepos.le,
% "the finding F about B is established" (or unsupported), with who found
% it and why. Criterion 2 and criteria A and C are what the record states
% — the demonstration and the tolerance of the device, the documented
% diagnosis (the shared template "the medical record of B documents C") and
% the treatment received, the pounds of traction ordered or documented (the
% threshold, 20, is in the rule) — as scenario facts. The alternatives A, B
% and C are read as hospital_beds.le reads its alternatives: what the record
% states (A, C) decides first, and only when the record states neither is
% the judgment (B) consulted — the "otherwise" is this model's device, so
% that a criterion the record establishes does not leave a judgment open
% beside it. The findings this policy reads, and the criterion each stands
% for:
%   impairment requiring cervical traction (1: a musculoskeletal or
%   neurologic impairment requiring traction equipment — ONE finding with
%   the kind of impairment as its reason); chin halter unusable (B: a
%   distortion of the lower jaw or neck anatomy, e.g. radical neck
%   dissection, such that a chin halter is unable to be utilized).
%
% Not modelled: the KX/GA/GZ modifiers of E0849 and E0855 (billing); the
% coding descriptions of the devices (E0849 must generate more than 20
% pounds and alternative vectors of force — coding). The Policy Article
% adds no documentation requirement of its own.

the target language is: prolog.

the templates are:
    % the record
    the appropriate use of *an item* was demonstrated to *a beneficiary*; undefined.
    *a beneficiary* tolerated *an item*; undefined.
    *a beneficiary* has received treatment for the temporomandibular joint condition; undefined.
    the treating practitioner orders or documents the medical necessity for *a number* pounds of cervical traction in the home; undefined.
    % derived
    *an item* is a higher force cervical traction device.
    *a beneficiary* meets the criteria for cervical traction with *an item*.
    the record of *a beneficiary* states an additional criterion for a higher force cervical traction device.
    *a beneficiary* meets an additional criterion for a higher force cervical traction device.

the knowledge base cervical_traction includes these resources:
    dmepos.

the knowledge base cervical_traction includes:

LCD L33823 is published at "https://www.cms.gov/medicare-coverage-database/view/lcd.aspx?lcdid=33823".
the text of LCD L33823 is at "sources/lcd/L33823.txt".
Policy Article A52476 is published at "https://www.cms.gov/medicare-coverage-database/view/article.aspx?articleid=52476".
the text of Policy Article A52476 is at "sources/article/A52476.txt".

% The two devices with additional criteria.
rule cervical_traction_higher_force with provenance LCD L33823,
        confer "Cervical traction devices described by code E0849 or E0855 are covered only when criteria 1 and 2 above and either criterion A, B or C below has been met":
an item is a higher force cervical traction device
    if the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and the code is in ["E0849", "E0855"].

% The codes this policy decides — outside the section checklist: a claim
% of another policy fails here without failing its own applicability.
% The codes this policy decides, and their benefit: durable medical
% equipment.
rule cervical_traction_codes with provenance Policy Article A52476,
        confer "Cervical traction devices are covered under the Durable Medical Equipment benefit":
the policy for code a code is cervical_traction
    if the code is in ["E0840", "E0849", "E0850", "E0855", "E0856", "E0860"].

section applicability is:

cervical_traction has no specific documentation requirements.

rule cervical_traction_benefit with provenance Policy Article A52476,
        confer "Cervical traction devices are covered under the Durable Medical Equipment benefit":
the benefit category of code a code is durable medical equipment
    if the policy for code the code is cervical_traction.

section question is:

% The over-the-door device (E0860): criteria 1 and 2.
rule cervical_traction_over_the_door with provenance LCD L33823,
        confer "Cervical traction devices (E0840, E0849, E0850, E0855 and E0860) are covered only if both of the following criteria are met":
a claim is reasonable and necessary
    if the claim is for an item
    and the HCPCS code of the item is "E0860"
    and the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the beneficiary meets the criteria for cervical traction with the item.

% The higher-force devices (E0849, E0855): criteria 1 and 2, and one of A,
% B, C.
rule cervical_traction_higher_force_covered with provenance LCD L33823,
        confer "Cervical traction devices described by code E0849 or E0855 are covered only when criteria 1 and 2 above and either criterion A, B or C below has been met":
a claim is reasonable and necessary
    if the claim is for an item
    and the item is a higher force cervical traction device
    and the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the beneficiary meets the criteria for cervical traction with the item
    and the beneficiary meets an additional criterion for a higher force cervical traction device.

% Criteria 1 and 2: the finding, the demonstration, the tolerance.
rule cervical_traction_criteria_1_and_2 with provenance LCD L33823,
        confer "The beneficiary has a musculoskeletal or neurologic impairment requiring traction equipment":
a beneficiary meets the criteria for cervical traction with an item
    if the finding impairment requiring cervical traction about the beneficiary is established
    and the appropriate use of the item was demonstrated to the beneficiary
    and the beneficiary tolerated the item.

% The additional criteria are alternatives: what the record states (A and
% C) decides first; only when the record states neither is the judgment (B)
% consulted.
rule cervical_traction_additional with provenance LCD L33823,
        confer "either criterion A, B or C below has been met":
a beneficiary meets an additional criterion for a higher force cervical traction device
    if the record of the beneficiary states an additional criterion for a higher force cervical traction device
    otherwise the finding chin halter unusable about the beneficiary is established.

% Criterion A: a treated temporomandibular joint dysfunction.
rule cervical_traction_criterion_a with provenance LCD L33823,
        confer "The beneficiary has a diagnosis of temporomandibular joint (TMJ) dysfunction; and has received treatment for the TMJ condition":
the record of a beneficiary states an additional criterion for a higher force cervical traction device
    if the medical record of the beneficiary documents temporomandibular joint dysfunction
    and the beneficiary has received treatment for the temporomandibular joint condition.

% Criterion B is the finding chin halter unusable, the "otherwise" line
% above; its passage: "The beneficiary has distortion of the lower jaw or
% neck anatomy (e.g., radical neck dissection) such that a chin halter is
% unable to be utilized".

% Criterion C: more than 20 pounds of traction in the home.
rule cervical_traction_criterion_c with provenance LCD L33823,
        confer "The treating practitioner orders and/or documents the medical necessity for greater than 20 pounds of cervical traction in the home setting":
the record of a beneficiary states an additional criterion for a higher force cervical traction device
    if the treating practitioner orders or documents the medical necessity for a number pounds of cervical traction in the home
    and the number > 20.

% No rule concludes E0840, E0850 ("If an E0840 or E0850 is ordered, it will
% be denied as not reasonable and necessary") or E0856 ("E0856 describes a
% cervical traction device that can be used with ambulation. Therefore, it
% will be denied as not reasonable and necessary").
